+# BEFORE patch.diff is applied, so it structurally cannot see prose that arrives in the
+# patch — a bundle can pass Check green and open a PR that immediately fails a required
+# status. Declare those commands here and the harness runs each one FROM a reconstructed
+# base + patch.diff tree, at two seams:
+#   * at Check, as gate rows (defaults: tier "T4", bundle scope) against the same lane
+#     worktree the bundle-scoped gates trust (#296) — a red lands in check-gates +
+#     SUMMARY §6 where sign-off sees it;
+#   * again in `{{ cli_name }} publish`, immediately before anything is pushed: the
+#     harness re-FETCHES, PINS the exact base commit the push will build on, materializes
+#     base + patch.diff in an ephemeral worktree at that commit, runs the commands there,
+#     and builds the pushed branch on that same commit — so a green certifies the very
+#     tree being pushed even when the base advanced since Check. ANY command that does
+#     not pass — any non-zero exit, exit 77 included — blocks the push (no branch, no
+#     PR) and is recorded in the bundle's host-ci.json naming the command and the base.
+# A bare string is shorthand for { cmd = "..." }; a table row may also set id / label /
+# tier. `gating` is forced true (the host's CI will fail the PR on these regardless, so
